---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import combiner from '../../generated/combiner.json';
import parameters from '../../generated/parameters.json';

// Generated JSON is imported only here, never from a .ts file (see the note in
// model-tool.ts), and handed to the island through two window globals.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const liveParameters = JSON.stringify(parameters);
const combinerData = JSON.stringify(combiner);
---

<Base
  title="Combine districts — Vermont School Budgets"
  description="Pick two or more Vermont school districts, pool them into one, and see each town's home tax rate if they were combined, with every step of the math shown."
>
  <h1>Combine districts</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Pick two or more school districts and treat them as one. See what each town's home tax rate
    would be if they were combined, with every step of the math shown. To change one district's
    numbers instead, use the <a href={`${base}/model/`}>What-if tool</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Many Vermont districts already share a <strong>supervisory union</strong> (a group of school
    districts that share one central office). This page goes further. It adds up the students and
    the spending of the districts you pick, as if they were one district. Then it works out the tax
    rate for every town in them, using the same steps the State uses.
  </p>
  <p>
    Students are counted by <strong>average daily membership</strong> (the average number of
    students enrolled across the school year). Then each town's rate is adjusted by its own
    number, called the <strong>common level of appraisal</strong> (how close the town's listed
    property values are to what homes really sell for).
  </p>

  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Read this before you use the numbers</strong>
    <p>
      For now, this page shows one thing: each town's rate if the districts were combined. It
      cannot show the rate today, or the change, yet. The State does not publish each district's own
      population density. It also does not publish each district's own count of state-placed
      students, students from lower-income homes, or English learners. The math for the rate today
      needs them, so this page does not show the rate today or the change. It will not fill those
      figures in for you.
    </p>
    <p>
      The “if combined” rate is what this tool shows. To see it, enter those figures for all the
      districts together, in the boxes below. What you enter is your own estimate, and the result
      depends heavily on it.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page's math does not match the rate the State published for every district. For 47 of
      the 97 districts that serve a single town, the published rate is lower than the one this math
      gives. So do not compare the “if combined” rate with the published rate. The table does not
      show the published rate beside it for that reason.
    </p>
    <p>
      The law's numbers this page uses for FY2026 were checked against the text of the law. A
      person has not yet signed off on that check.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div id="combiner-link-notes"></div>

  <form id="combiner-form">
    <fieldset class="field-group">
      <legend>Which year</legend>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-year">Fiscal year</label>
          <select id="combiner-year"></select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="field-help">
        Only FY2026 can be run for now. It is the only year with each town's common level of
        appraisal in this build. Other years show here but cannot be picked.
      </p>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="field-group">
      <legend>Which districts</legend>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-grouping">Start from a merger study group (optional)</label>
          <select id="combiner-grouping">
            <option value="">— none —</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="field-help">
        Act 170 of 2026 put districts into groups that study joining into larger ones. These are
        the 18 groups on the state's first list from September 18, 2026. Picking a group fills in
        its districts. You can then add or take out districts. To read more,
        see <a href={`${base}/groupings/`}>merger study groups</a>. Some groups have districts that can't
        be combined yet, because the State withheld some of their student counts. For example,
        Slate Valley's union district can't be combined yet for that reason.
      </p>
      <p id="combiner-grouping-status" class="field-help" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

      <h3 id="combiner-picked-heading" class="combiner-subhead" tabindex="-1">Your districts</h3>
      <div id="combiner-picked"></div>

      <h3 class="combiner-subhead">Add districts, by supervisory union</h3>
      <p class="field-help">
        Open a supervisory union to see its districts. A district that is greyed out can't be
        combined yet. The reason is written under it.
      </p>
      <div id="combiner-picker" class="combiner-picker"></div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="field-group">
      <legend>Spending</legend>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-factor">Spending factor</label>
          <input id="combiner-factor" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="field-help">
        1 means the combined district spends the same total as the districts spend now. 0.95 means
        5% less, and 1.05 means 5% more. It starts at 1, so any change in spending is one you chose.
      </p>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="field-group">
      <legend>Act 84 decrease (an assumption)</legend>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-act84">Pooled Act 84 decrease, dollars per $100</label>
          <input id="combiner-act84" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="field-help">
        Act 84 of 2024 gives some districts a short-term cut in their tax rate. The cut shrinks each
        year until 2029. For “today,” each district's own cut is used. No one has said what cut a
        combined district would get, so this starts at 0. This is a guess, not a published figure.
        Enter it in dollars per $100 of property value (13 cents is 0.13).
      </p>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="field-group">
      <legend>Figures the State does not publish</legend>
      <p class="field-help">
        Each of these changes how students are counted. Leave a box blank and the result names it
        as missing. The page will not fill it in for you. What you enter is your own estimate, and
        the result depends heavily on it.
      </p>
      <p class="field-help">
        The three student boxes take a number of students, not a percent.
      </p>
      <p id="combiner-adm-scale" class="field-help"></p>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-density">Population density, people per square mile</label>
          <input id="combiner-density" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
          <small class="field-help">
            How spread out people are (the law calls this sparsity), for the combined district.
          </small>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-state-placed">State-placed students, a number of students</label>
          <input id="combiner-state-placed" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
          <small class="field-help">
            No published per-district figure. Enter the total number for all the districts
            together, not a percent, or leave blank.
          </small>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-poverty">Students from lower-income homes, a number of students</label>
          <input id="combiner-poverty" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
          <small class="field-help">
            Students at or below 185% of the federal poverty level. No published per-district
            figure. Enter the total number for all the districts together, not a percent, or leave
            blank.
          </small>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-el">English learners, a number of students</label>
          <input id="combiner-el" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
          <small class="field-help">
            No published per-district figure. Enter the total number for all the districts
            together, not a percent, or leave blank.
          </small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="field-group">
      <legend>A small school (optional)</legend>
      <p class="field-help">
        A very small school can add to the student count. Leave these blank if none of the schools
        is small. If you name one, also say which district it is in.
      </p>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-school">School name</label>
          <input id="combiner-school" type="text" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-enrollment">Average enrollment over two years, a number of students</label>
          <input id="combiner-enrollment" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-school-in">In which district</label>
          <select id="combiner-school-in"></select>
        </div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="field-group">
      <legend>Statewide average</legend>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="combiner-avg">Statewide average spending per weighted student, dollars</label>
          <input id="combiner-avg" type="number" min="0" step="any" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="field-help">
        Filled in from the State's published FY2026 figure. You can change it.
      </p>
    </fieldset>
  </form>

  <div class="share-tools">
    <button type="button" id="combiner-share">Copy shareable link</button>
    <span id="combiner-share-status" class="share-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
  </div>

  <h2>Result</h2>
  <p id="combiner-result-status" class="field-help" role="status"></p>
  <div id="combiner-result"></div>

  <h2>What this tool will not do</h2>
  <p>
    It does not rank groupings, score them, or call any result a “saving.” A rate that goes up and
    a rate that goes down are shown the same way, with a plus or minus sign and plain words. It
    does not pick a “best” grouping. It will not fill in a figure the State does not publish. Any
    such figure on this page was entered by a person, and the result depends heavily on it.
  </p>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .combiner-subhead {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .combiner-rate-warning {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .combiner-picker details.combiner-su {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
  }
  .combiner-picker details.combiner-su > summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .combiner-picker .combiner-add-su {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0.2rem;
  }
  .combiner-district-list,
  .combiner-picked-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .combiner-district-list li,
  .combiner-picked-list li {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .combiner-district-list li.combiner-blocked label {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .combiner-picked-list .combiner-remove {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
    margin-left: 0.4rem;
  }
  .combiner-message {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .combiner-towns td,
  .combiner-towns th {
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .combiner-towns td.combiner-change {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .combiner-towns td.combiner-change .combiner-why > summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .combiner-towns td.combiner-change .field-help {
    white-space: normal;
    min-width: 18rem;
  }
  .combiner-math-row > td {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  details.combiner-math > summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .combiner-members .combiner-pooled-row th,
  .combiner-members .combiner-pooled-row td {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .combiner-assumptions li,
  .combiner-blockers li {
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
  }
</style>

<script define:vars={{ liveParameters, combinerData }}>
  window.__VT_PARAMETERS__ = JSON.parse(liveParameters);
  window.__VT_COMBINER__ = JSON.parse(combinerData);
</script>

<script>
  import { initCombinerTool } from '../../scripts/combiner-tool';
  initCombinerTool(
    window.__VT_PARAMETERS__ ?? [],
    window.__VT_COMBINER__ ?? { fiscal_year: 2026, districts: {}, towns: {}, sus: {}, groupings: [] },
  );
</script>
